BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF WONOGIRI,

Considering : a. that based on Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;

b. that to realize the provision of protection for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children as well as to provide legal certainty particularly in the implementation of child protection in Wonogiri Regency, it is necessary to regulate this in a Regional Regulation;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in point a and point b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Violence Against Children.

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 13 Year 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas Within Central Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 42);

3. Law Number 4 Year 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);

4. Law Number 7 Year 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3668);

5. Law Number 4 Year 1997 concerning Persons with Disabilities (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1997 Number 9, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3670);

6. Law Number 20 Year 1999 concerning Ratification of the ILO Convention Concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);

7. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

8. Law Number 1 Year 2000 concerning Ratification of the ILO Convention Concerning the Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labour (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2000 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);

9. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);

10. Law Number 13 Year 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);

11. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

12. Law Number 32 Year 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 12 Year 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 Year 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);

13. Law Number 13 Year 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);

14. Law Number 21 Year 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

15. Law Number 12 Year 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);

16. Law Number 11 Year 2012 concerning the Juvenile Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);

17. Government Regulation Number 2 Year 1988 concerning Welfare Efforts for Children with Problems (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1988 Number 2, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3367);

18. Government Regulation Number 79 Year 2005 concerning Guidelines for Development and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2005 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4593);

19. Government Regulation Number 38 Year 2007 concerning the Division of Government Affairs Between the Government, Provincial Regional Government, and Regency/Municipal Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4737);

20. Government Regulation Number 9 Year 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);

21. Presidential Regulation Number 1 Year 2007 concerning Ratification, Promulgation, and Dissemination of Legislation;

22. Presidential Decree Number 36 Year 1990 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Rights of the Child;

23. Presidential Decree Number 88 Year 2002 concerning the National Action Plan for the Elimination of Trafficking in Women and Children;

24. Regional Regulation of Central Java Province Number 3 Year 2009 concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Violence Against Children;

With Mutual Approval
THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF WONOGIRI REGENCY
And

CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 6
(1) Victims of gender-based violence and child victims of violence have the right to obtain:
a. protection from family, police, prosecution, courts, advocates, social institutions or other parties either temporarily or based on a protection order from the court;
b. obtain protection for personal security, family, and property, and freedom from threats related to testimony that will be, is being, or has been given;
c. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
d. freedom from ensnaring questions;
e. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;
f. obtain services that are fast, appropriate, comfortable, and according to needs.
g. health services in accordance with medical needs;
h. special handling related to victim confidentiality;
i. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations and spiritual guidance services;
j. recovery and social reintegration;
k. obtain legal, psychological, spiritual, economic, and social assistance.
(2) The rights of victims as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of applicable laws and regulations.

CHAPTER VI
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 7
(1) The obligations of the Regional Government include:
a. preventing the occurrence of violence;
b. providing protection for victims of violence; c. providing recovery services and social reintegration; d. encouraging and increasing community participation; e. conducting cooperation with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence; and
f. supervising the implementation of services for victims with service standards that involve the community;
(2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:
a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based and child violence;
b. establish and facilitate the implementation of integrated services;
c. provide facilities and infrastructure;
d. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
e. conduct coordination and cooperation in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based and child violence;
f. encourage community participation; and
g. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) The Regional Government in carrying out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

